{"name":"Piglet","hex":"#ffc0c6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Piglet","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An innocent and naive person."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Piglet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pig","blocks":[{"text":"The pig, also called swine or hog, is an omnivorous, domesticated, even-toed, hoofed mammal. It is named the domestic pig when distinguishing it from other members of the genus Sus. Some authorities consider it a subspecies of Sus scrofa ; other authorities consider it a distinct species. Pigs were domesticated independently twice during the Neolithic, in the Near East around the Tigris Basin, and in China. When domesticated pigs arrived in Europe from the Near East, they extensively interbred with wild boar in Europe but retained their domesticated features."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Pig_farm_Vampula_1.jpg/330px-Pig_farm_Vampula_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pig","wikidata":"Q787"},{"title":"Suckling pig","blocks":[{"text":"A sucking-pig (BrE) or suckling pig (AmE) is a piglet fed on its mother's milk. In culinary contexts, a sucking-pig is slaughtered before the end of its second month. Celebrated since Greek and Roman times, it is traditionally cooked whole, usually roasted, in various cuisines, and is often prepared for special occasions and gatherings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Cochinillos-Mercado_de_la_Cebada.jpg/330px-Cochinillos-Mercado_de_la_Cebada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suckling_pig","wikidata":"Q23015"},{"title":"Piglet (Winnie-the-Pooh)","blocks":[{"text":"Piglet is a fictional character from A. A. Milne's Winnie-the-Pooh books. Piglet is Winnie‑the‑Pooh's closest friend amongst all the toys and animals featured in the stories. Although he is a \"Very Small Animal\" of a generally timid disposition, he tries to be brave and on occasion conquers his fears."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Piglet_EHShepard.jpg/330px-Piglet_EHShepard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piglet_(Winnie-the-Pooh)","wikidata":"Q836719"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Su%C3%ADno_alta_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Su%C3%ADno_alta_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Su%C3%ADno_alta_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Su%C3%ADno_alta_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Su%C3%ADno_alta_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Su%C3%ADno_alta_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASu%C3%ADno_alta_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Domestic_pig_skull_%28cropped%29.jpeg/250px-Domestic_pig_skull_%28cropped%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Domestic_pig_skull_%28cropped%29.jpeg/500px-Domestic_pig_skull_%28cropped%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Domestic_pig_skull_%28cropped%29.jpeg/250px-Domestic_pig_skull_%28cropped%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADomestic_pig_skull_(cropped).jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Pig_hand_skeleton_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Pig_hand_skeleton_%2